content:
E31 shows 190 orphaned orders (more than the 140 in the signal, and growing). E32 shows all messages created during the outage window are in state "done" — meaning the messages exist but the orders are still not fulfilled. This suggests the orders have no messages at all (the messages query in E31 filters for pending/processing, and E32 shows none exist in those states from that window). The orphaned orders likely have either no message, or a message in a terminal/failed state other than done.

Let me check whether these orphaned orders have messages in any state (including failed/dead) to confirm they truly lack live messages, and also check if the count is still growing (new orders being created faster than worker can process).

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT m.state, COUNT(DISTINCT o.id) as order_cnt FROM orders o LEFT JOIN messages m ON m.order_id = o.id WHERE o.status NOT IN ('fulfilled','paid','complete') GROUP BY m.state",
      "why": "Determine whether unfulfilled orders have no message at all (NULL state) vs. messages in failed/dead states, to confirm requeue_orphaned_orders covers all 190 cases."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "service": "worker",
      "kind": "bad_deploy",
      "mechanism": "Worker v1.0.1 deployed at t=564 caused repeated health-check failures and restarts from t=592–t=659, preventing queue consumption; orders created during this window were never picked up within the 2-minute SLA, and even after rollback the backlog of orphaned orders (now 190, still growing per E31 vs E1) has not been re-enqueued.",
      "supporting": ["E1", "E10", "E11", "E12", "E14", "E15", "E31", "E32"],
      "refuting": [],
      "explains": ["I2_no_orphaned_orders"],
      "repair_plan": [
        {
          "action": "requeue_orphaned_orders",
          "params": {}
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Worker v1.0.1 crash-looped from t=592–t=659 leaving orders unprocessed; rollback fixed the worker but 190 orphaned orders still lack live queue messages and need requeue_orphaned_orders to recover."
}
